NH doesn't really have a way to use up "part of a turn", the best it
can do is use up a whole turn with a fractional probablility instead;
on average that comes out the same.

Trying to do things you cannot do is frequently "free" in terms of a
time step; exploring Mines while blind would take three times as long
otherwise, but trying to walk through a wall is "free", making blind
mapping pretty cheap.

There isn't really any way to convert this conceptually to "real life"
AD&D motion, where each grid cell is conceptually about ten feet or
three meters across, since walking from the middle to the edge of such
a cell to "push" an immovable boulder, then returning to the center
should surely take the same amount of time as crossing a cell.

